/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 113 0 R
/T (1.1: PROBLEM STATEMENT Manually controlled or tethered robotic arms impose constraints on portability and ease of use. The objective of this project is to develop a compact robotic gripper arm that can be operated wirelessly via Bluetooth from an Android device, providing flexible and intuitive control of six servo joints and a gripper without any physical connection between the controller and the arm.)
/E (1.1: PROBLEM STATEMENT Manually controlled or tethered robotic arms impose constraints on portability and ease of use. The objective of this project is to develop a compact robotic gripper arm that can be operated wirelessly via Bluetooth from an Android device, providing flexible and intuitive control of six servo joints and a gripper without any physical connection between the controller and the arm.)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
