/Title (1.4.6: Gripper Mechanism The end-effector is a two-finger parallel gripper driven by a single SG90 micro servo. A rack-and-pinion or lever-linkage mechanism converts the servo's rotational output into the linear opening/closing motion of the fingers. The gripper can handle objects up to approximately 60 mm in diameter and exert a gripping force sufficient for lightweight pick-and-place tasks.)
